Subject: Can we use covariate without order for LOCO
Message-ID: <B8bhanMaJlo.2jvLT3LTBgAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/B8bhanMaJlo/m/2jvLT3LTBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Karl

I'm using R/qtl2 for a 4-way mapping population for which I have phenotypes for few sites. I want to use site as a covariate. As far I understand R/qtl2 can only use numeric covariate. For my case as we have more that two sites, if I want to convert it to numeric, this will be ordered. Can it be possible in R/qtl2 to fit a LOCO model so that I can use these sites as a covariate but without order?

Best,
Taslima

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Fri Jan  4 12:01:48 2019
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Fri, 04 Jan 2019 12:01:48 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl2-disc] Can we use covariate without order for LOCO
Message-ID: <B8bhanMaJlo.ZXUkI0ZBCwAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <B8bhanMaJlo.2jvLT3LTBgAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <B8bhanMaJlo.2jvLT3LTBgAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/B8bhanMaJlo/m/ZXUkI0ZBCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You need to turn it into a 0/1 matrix, where each column represents a site, with values 1 for the individuals in that site and 0 otherwise. You need a matrix with one fewer columns than you have sites.

You can use the function model.matrix() to construct this.
If x is your covariate, something like this:

    x_factor <- factor(x)
    x_matrix <- model.matrix( ~ x_factor)[ , -1]

karl

